Z||000000||AL||02-22-2001||11:09 PM||||my winshield pump doesn't shoot water,and my courtesy light inside the hood don't work.both are new,fuses are good also,just to tired to trace wires.<p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 02-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||02-23-2001||07:01 AM||||Did you check for power at the pump with a meter?<BR>I think that the parking lights have to be on for the under hood(front hood)light to work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||02-23-2001||10:37 AM||||yes, the little courtesy bulb will not come on unless the parking lights are on.  Mine wouldnt work at all, so I tested for ground, and the ground wasnt there at all, even though all the wire that I could trace back through the loom was perfect.  So, I just added a new wire and gave it a new ground to (I think) one of the mounting bolts that holds on the jack bracket.<P>Can you hear the wiper fluid motor running when you hit the "wash"?  Check the connections right there if not.<P>If it is running, make sure that none of the hoses are clogged somehow, pinched, or even severed.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||02-23-2001||02:24 PM||||How would one unclog the washer lines? My washer worked fine before te engine blew and it sat for 6 months, now I can hear the pump but no juice. I'm pretty sure it's clogged.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2xsess||02-23-2001||02:31 PM||||<BR>Stimpy, it's most likely your nozzles that are clogged, I've used needles to clean those out.<P>Sorry, AL, don't have any info for your problem||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||02-23-2001||09:54 PM||||i know that the parking lights have to be on,but i was just wondering if someone could give me a quick fixs, guess i will have to test the wires with my meter.<p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 02-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||JetroGT||02-24-2001||04:21 PM||||When rebuilding the front end of the GT my parking lights did not work. It was a bad ground in one of the front P-light sockets. I had to get a new socket from the junk yard. <BR>Check for corosion in the bulb sockets. The washer pump still dosent work on the GT. I traced it to the steering column switch but still haven't replaced it. ||||reg||4
